# Interruption Logging

**Applies to**: All agents and the orchestrator

## When to Log

Log to `artefacts/build/agent-interruptions.md` immediately when:

| Type | Who logs | Trigger |
|------|----------|---------|
| Question | Agent | Blocked, needs external answer |
| Tool approval | Agent | User prompted for permission |
| Wrong approach | Orchestrator | Agent started wrong direction, required correction |
| Missing context | Orchestrator | Agent failed because context bundle was insufficient |
| Standards violation | Reviewer | Agent used wrong tool/command, caught in review |

## When NOT to Log

- Autonomous decisions (tool choice, code style, minor trade-offs)
- Self-resolved issues (lint fixes, command syntax corrections)
- Only log when external attention was required or given

## Format

See `context/standards/agent-standards.md` §3.6 for entry format.
